  "question": {
    "text": "A point charge +q is placed at the origin. A second point charge +9 q is placed at $(\\mathrm{d}, 0,0)$ in Cartesian coordinate system. The point in between them where the electric field vanishes is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eYBV4",
      "text": "$(4 \\mathrm{~d} / 3,0,0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QkBff",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{d} / 4,0,0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r7sHt",
      "text": "$(3 \\mathrm{~d} / 4,0,0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cPByq",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{d} / 3,0,0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EUmMu4RcgtNDEvOJCCTkUJrjF12MIvk59VVWSudZl2Y.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>Let $\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{p}}=0$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{kq}}{\\mathrm{x}^2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{k} 9 \\mathrm{q}}{(\\mathrm{~d}-\\mathrm{x})^2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{~d}-\\mathrm{x}}{\\mathrm{x}}=3 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{4}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\therefore$ co-ordinate of P is $\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{4}, 0,0\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
